---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
import InteractiveTerminal from '../components/InteractiveTerminal.astro';
import LivingLoop from '../components/LivingLoop.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="DeJon Gaines | Technology Transformation Leader" 
    description="Enterprise AI by day. Personal AI by conviction."
>
  <!-- Navigation -->
  <nav>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="nav-content">
        <a href="/" class="logo">DG</a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="#about">About</a>
          <a href="#focus">Focus</a>
          <a href="#lab">The Lab</a>
          <a href="#notes">Field Notes</a>
          <a href="#events">Events</a>
          <a href="#engage">Connect</a>
          <button id="theme-toggle" class="theme-toggle" aria-label="Toggle dark mode">🌙</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-content">
            <h1><span class="gradient-name">DeJon Gaines</span></h1>
            <div class="subtitle">Chief Technology Officer | AI &amp; CX Transformation</div>
            <div class="subtitle-alt">Enterprise AI by day. Personal AI by conviction.</div>
            <p class="tagline">
              Digital transformation used to mean 18-month roadmaps and PowerPoint milestones. Now I watch enterprises generate measurable value in days, sometimes hours.
            </p>
            <p class="tagline">
              But the shift I can't stop thinking about is smaller, and closer to home: what happens when one person puts real AI infrastructure into their own life. Not a chatbot tab in a browser — an AI chief of staff I built and host myself, running on a supercomputer next to my desk.
            </p>
            <p class="tagline">
              That's the experiment I'm living. This site is where I write down what I'm learning.
            </p>
            <div class="impact-areas">
              <span class="impact-item">Rapid Value Delivery</span>
              <span class="impact-item">AI at Scale</span>
              <span class="impact-item">Culture &amp; Change</span>
              <span class="impact-item">Executive Leadership</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hero-cta">
              <a href="#engage" class="btn btn-primary">Let's Talk</a>
              <a href="#lab" class="btn btn-outline">See the Lab</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-terminal">
            <Terminal />
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- About Section -->
    <section id="about" style="background: var(--bg-secondary); padding: 4rem 0;">
      <div class="container">
        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 400px 1fr; gap: 4rem; max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; align-items: center;">
          
          <img src="/techworld.png" alt="DeJon Gaines at Lenovo Tech World" style="
              width: 100%; 
              height: 450px; 
              border-radius: 12px; 
              object-fit: cover; 
              box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.2);
          ">
          
          <div>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
              I've spent twenty years inside technology transformations — first watching the analog world go digital in the early 2000s, then helping thousands of commercial and public-sector clients navigate what came after. The lesson never changed: transformation is never just about technology. It's about timing, scale, and adaptability.
            </p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
              Lately the most interesting timing question isn't in the enterprise at all. Enterprises adopt AI with committees, pilots, and procurement cycles. A person adopts AI at the speed of curiosity. The gap between those two speeds is where I spend most of my thinking — because the individual who runs their life on AI today is the customer, employee, and executive every company will meet tomorrow.
            </p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem;">
              So I run the experiment on myself. My calendar, inbox, research, and household operations run through an AI I built and host at home. It makes me sharper at the day job, and it makes me a more honest advisor: I never recommend a pattern I haven't lived with.
            </p>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
              20+ years enterprise technology · McKinsey Executive Leadership program · Lexington, Kentucky
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Current Focus Section -->
    <section id="focus">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>What I'm Exploring Now</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          The questions I'm actively testing, and the conversations I'm having with leaders who want more than vendor promises.
        </p>
        
        <div class="card-grid">
          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">Agentic AI in Production</h3>
            <p class="card-description">
              Live-call handling agents with autonomous decision-making, deployed in real contact-center environments. The platforms have shipped; the scarce skill now is operating them — tuning against live conversations, proving quality with evidence, earning the right to automate the next call type. The gap between demo and production is where most AI initiatives die; I work in that gap.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">The Small Model Thesis</h3>
            <p class="card-description">
              Purpose-trained 14B-class models are outperforming giants on domain-specific work — faster inference, better economics. The same thesis powers my house: small local models handle voice and latency-sensitive work; frontier models handle heavy reasoning. Purpose-trained beats general-purpose at production scale, whether production is a call center or a kitchen.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card">
            <h3 class="card-title">AI in Everyday Life</h3>
            <p class="card-description">
              The most under-reported AI story is personal: people quietly using AI to manage health, money, family logistics, and learning. I'm building and documenting a full personal AI stack — and mapping what individual adoption tells us about where the enterprise wave goes next.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 3rem; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-secondary); border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
          <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
            These questions drive my keynotes, advisory work, and the experiments running in my lab. If you're past the theoretical frameworks and want a conversation grounded in what actually works, <a href="#engage" style="color: var(--text-primary); font-weight: 600;">let's connect</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  <!-- The Lab Section -->
<section class="ai-lab" id="lab">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>🧪 The Lab</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">This is where I pressure-test what everyone else is pitching. Real hardware, real workloads, real results — not vendor demos.</p>

    <p class="lab-intro">
      Most AI labs live in datacenters. Mine lives in my home office in Lexington: an NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10, 128GB unified memory) running a stack I've built to answer one question — how much of a life can one person delegate to AI they own and host themselves?
    </p>

    <LivingLoop />

    <p class="ll-caption">
      A conversation is the inner loop: speech in, reasoning across knowledge, memory, and tools, speech out — in under a second. The outer loop is what separates a production system from a demo: every conversation is captured and scored against evidence, and what's learned flows back in — better prompts, better routing, better answers. The next conversation is better than the last, provably, release over release. And the same two loops run at both scales: enterprise, and the machine next to my desk.
    </p>

    <div class="cos-block">
      <h3>The chief-of-staff experiment</h3>
      <p>
        The centerpiece is an AI chief of staff I built and host myself. It talks with me in real time — a voice loop with sub-3-second round-trips, running entirely on local models, so the conversation never leaves the house — and it quietly keeps the operational side of my life moving so my attention goes where it matters.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-stats">
      <div class="lab-stat"><span class="ls-v">&lt;3s</span><span class="ls-k">voice round-trip, fully local</span></div>
      <div class="lab-stat"><span class="ls-v">128GB</span><span class="ls-k">unified memory at the edge</span></div>
      <div class="lab-stat"><span class="ls-v">0</span><span class="ls-k">cloud round-trips required for a conversation</span></div>
      <div class="lab-stat"><span class="ls-v">1</span><span class="ls-k">human, many agents</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="explore-grid">
      <div class="explore-card"><h4>🎙️ Conversational AI at the Edge</h4><p>Full voice pipelines running on local hardware. No cloud round-trips, no per-call API costs, no data leaving the building. Testing where the performance ceiling actually is.</p></div>
      <div class="explore-card"><h4>🤖 AI Workflow Automation</h4><p>Exploring how AI agents can handle complex, multi-step processes in enterprise environments — reducing integration timelines from months to weeks. Particularly focused on what this unlocks in regulated industries like healthcare and government.</p></div>
      <div class="explore-card"><h4>💰 The Real Economics of Inference</h4><p>Running production workloads locally to answer the questions vendors won't: actual cost per interaction, break-even points between on-prem and cloud, and where data sovereignty becomes non-negotiable.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="lab-footnote">
      <p>The same architecture patterns — edge inference, agent orchestration, small-model economics — are what I deploy for enterprises through Digital Gaines LLC: conversational AI platforms in weeks, not quarters, at 40–60% lower inference cost.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

    <!-- Field Notes Section -->
    <section id="notes">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Field Notes</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          Writing from inside the experiment — what the personal AI stack actually does, what it costs, and what it predicts. <span class="notes-soon">Coming soon.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="notes-grid">
          <article class="note-card">
            <span class="note-badge">Coming soon</span>
            <h3>"I Hired an AI Chief of Staff. I Also Built It."</h3>
            <p>What changes when your assistant lives in your house, not in a browser tab.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="note-card">
            <span class="note-badge">Coming soon</span>
            <h3>"The Kitchen-Table Datacenter"</h3>
            <p>What a DGX Spark at home actually costs, actually does, and actually can't.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="note-card">
            <span class="note-badge">Coming soon</span>
            <h3>"Enterprises Buy AI. People Adopt It."</h3>
            <p>Why individual adoption runs years ahead of corporate adoption, and what that predicts.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

<!-- Events Section -->
<section id="events" style="background: var(--bg-secondary);">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Events</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      Where I'll be, and where I've been. Pressure-testing new ideas and connecting with leaders who are building, not just buying.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">Upcoming</p>

    <div class="card-grid">
      <!-- Genesys Xperience -->
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid #00a4ef;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
          <span style="font-size: 2rem;">🌐</span>
          <div>
            <h3 class="card-title" style="margin: 0;">Genesys Xperience</h3>
            <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0;">September 1–3, 2026 | Wynn Las Vegas | Las Vegas, NV</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="card-description">
          The CX+AI Event of the Year. Genesys Xperience brings together the practitioners, architects, and leaders shaping the next generation of customer experience. A chance to see where conversational AI and cloud contact center technology intersect in production at scale.
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top: 1rem;">
          <span style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.85rem;">📍 Wynn Las Vegas</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="booking-line">
      <a href="#engage"><em>Booking Q4 2026 / 2027 — speaking on agentic AI and personal AI infrastructure →</em></a>
    </p>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-primary); border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
        <strong style="color: var(--text-primary);">Attending one of these events?</strong> I'm always up for a conversation with leaders who are building something real. Let's connect.
      </p>
      <a href="#engage" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Get in Touch</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Recent engagements -->
    <div style="margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-color);">
      <p style="font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Recent</p>
      <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
        <li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">CCW Las Vegas 2026 — June 2026 · Las Vegas, NV</li>
        <li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Microsoft AI Tour — April 29, 2026 · Atlanta, GA</li>
        <li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">Microsoft AI Tour — January 21, 2026 · New York, NY</li>
        <li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);">The DEX Advantage — January 14, 2026 · Cincinnati, OH</li>
        <li style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding: 0.5rem 0;">Lenovo Tech World @ CES — January 6, 2026 · Las Vegas, NV</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

    <!-- Engage Section -->
    <section id="engage">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Let's Connect</h2>
        <div class="engage-content">
          <p class="section-intro">
            The best insights I've gained have come from conversations with people solving hard problems. If you're navigating transformation, exploring AI strategy, or just want to exchange ideas, I'm always open to connecting.
          </p>
          <div class="card-grid">
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="card-title">Speaking &amp; Workshops</h3>
              <p class="card-description">
                Agentic AI in production, the small-model thesis, and a newer talk I'm loving: what happens when AI moves into everyday life.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="card-title">Advisory</h3>
              <p class="card-description">
                AI strategy, platform modernization, and CX transformation through Digital Gaines LLC.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <h3 class="card-title">Peer Conversations</h3>
              <p class="card-description">
                If you're running your own personal-AI experiment, I want to compare notes. Seriously.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="contact-info">
            <p class="location">Based in Lexington, Kentucky</p>
            <div class="contact-buttons">
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dejon-gaines" target="_blank" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
              <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dejon-gaines" target="_blank" class="btn btn-outline">LinkedIn</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="footer-content">
        <div class="footer-copyright">
          © 2026 DeJon Gaines. All rights reserved.
        </div>
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/dejon-gaines" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>
          </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>
  <InteractiveTerminal />

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap');

  /* ---- Hero ---- */
  .subtitle-alt {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-content .tagline { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .hero-content .tagline:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  /* ---- The Lab ---- */
  .ai-lab { background: var(--bg-secondary); }
  .ai-lab h2 { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; text-align: center; }
  .ai-lab h2::after { left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); }
  .ai-lab .section-intro { text-align: center; max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem; }

  .lab-intro {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .ll-caption {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 1.75rem auto 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cos-block {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-left: 4px solid #2fd57b;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
  .cos-block h3 {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .cos-block p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }

  .lab-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .lab-stat {
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 12px;
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .ls-v {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .ls-k { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.5; }

  .explore-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .explore-card { padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-primary); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); transition: border-color 0.3s, transform 0.2s; }
  .explore-card:hover { border-color: rgba(59,130,246,0.35); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .explore-card h4 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .explore-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }

  .lab-footnote {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--accent-color);
  }
  .lab-footnote p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0; }

  /* ---- Field Notes ---- */
  .notes-soon {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .notes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(290px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
  .note-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 12px;
    transition: border-color 0.3s, transform 0.2s;
  }
  .note-card:hover { border-color: var(--accent-color); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .note-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .note-card h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); line-height: 1.45; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .note-card p { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }

  /* ---- Connect ---- */
  .contact-buttons { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1rem; }

  /* ---- Events ---- */
  .booking-line { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .booking-line a { color: var(--text-secondary); text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .booking-line a:hover { color: var(--accent-color); }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .explore-grid, .notes-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .lab-stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
</Layout>
